  "complexity": 4,
  "title": "Bugfix: evidence feedback loop: specialist.shared_evidence lists the goal pool into every packet and spawn re-adds each line as a previous_result row with a fresh index (12,292 rows, 2.3 MB packets)",
  "spec": "Root cause found by the Planner (real 22:15): in spawn._packet_body, when skills mode is active, composition.shared_evidence(task) appends one evidence line per item of the goal evidence pool; every line is then turned into a previous_result evidence object with location task:<id>:evidence:<index> and added to the same pool, so each packet build grows the pool by the number of lines it read (T-1274 alone contributed 3,034 rows; the pool reached 12,292 rows and a review packet rendered 2.26 MB, argv too long). Fix: (1) previous_result rows are keyed by (task id, content hash) with no running index, and EvidencePool.add replaces the existing row for a task instead of appending; rows for superseded tasks are dropped on load; (2) shared_evidence output never becomes new evidence objects (do not wrap lines that already came from the pool); (3) cap the legacy evidence section and the shared_evidence contribution at [context_router].legacy_evidence_chars (default 6000, dated comment) so no mode can build an unbounded packet. Regression tests: building three packets in a row for one task leaves the pool size unchanged; a pool with 5,000 rows yields an evidence section under the cap. Repository rules: unittest, no new dependencies, run .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh . until green, do not ask questions.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_evidence.py::test_previous_result_rows_keyed_per_task_and_superseded_dropped",
    "tests/test_spawn.py::test_three_packet_builds_do_not_grow_the_pool_and_evidence_section_capped",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh exits 0"
  ],
  "scope": [
